<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23046" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-excūsābĭlis</span></b> ,
			e, adj., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>that cannot be excused</i>, <i>inexcusable</i> (<b>poet.</b> and
			post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ne te retrahas, et inexcusabilis absis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 18, 58</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tempus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					7, 511</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">onera,</span>”
				<i>that cannot be refused</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Dig.
					5, 1, 50</span></i>
			: necessitas, Cod. Th. 11, 16, 7 al.—<i>Comp.</i>, <i><span class="en">Ambros. de Vocat. Gent. 2,
			4</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
